:: The Calendar [event mom_quest] {"position":"4775,1075","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Calendar" (mom_calendar), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 5.9. Her milestone into corruption stage 3 (Complicit), the biggest
   mom scene of Stage 1. She keeps the shared calendar, and she has noticed that her "bad days" line up with the days the
   office feels different and with the test sessions. She doesn't rage. She puts a printout on my desk with the pattern
   circled and asks: "Is it the box?" A reversal: for once she has turned the table.
   The choice sets $mom.flags.calendarChoice:
     "truth"   part of it, not the sabotage. She needs to think. Then: she can't tell how much is her and how much is the
               box, and she's decided she doesn't care
     "anchor"  the Anchor (setup.useDevice valenxAnchor, a use, the whole charge, a spike in its log) plants one belief:
               this is your choice, and you love it. A nosebleed. Afterwards I text $ethan.name a hint, and he answers
               with a joke. He has already seen the spike
   The quest's set unlocks Whenever ($mom.flags.freeUse). That night I test it: the hallway, no device, "Whatever you need." */
<<silent>>
	<<SetBackground $locations[14].img>>
	<<set _calAnchor to $company.devices.valenxAnchor>>
	<<set _calAnchorOk to (_calAnchor.owned and setup.deviceUsesLeft(_calAnchor) > 0 and _calAnchor.charge >= $company.impactCost[10])>>
<</silent>>
$mom.callName has been quiet all week, the busy kind of quiet, not the sad kind. She's stayed late three nights in a row with the shared calendar open on both her monitors, scrolling back through months of it, and every time I walked past she minimized the window.

This morning she comes to my desk with a single sheet of paper and puts it face down in front of me, squared to the edge of the desk. Then she sits in the chair next to it with her hands folded in her lap.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Can you look at that for me, honey? When you have a minute." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Turn it over">>
It's a printout of the company calendar, three months of it shrunk down to fit one page, every day a little colored box. She's gone over it by hand with three highlighters.

Yellow is for the days the office felt "warm", her word, written in the margin: the days everyone worked late without complaining. Orange is the evening test sessions in the meeting room. Pink is what she's labeled, in tiny careful letters, <i>bad days</i>, the days she came home and cleaned the kitchen until midnight, and the days she knocked on my door.

The pink is almost always on an orange day, or on the day after a yellow one. She has drawn neat little lines between them, and circled the clusters, the way she'd circle a scheduling conflict for a client.

<<Media "images/characters/mom/events/the_calendar/printout.jpg" 600>>
/* A calendar printout on a desk, highlighted in yellow, orange and pink, neat circles and lines drawn between the days */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "I've spent a lot of years keeping other people's calendars, sweetie, and if there's one thing I'm good at, it's noticing when something keeps landing on the same days." },
{ text: "She isn't angry. That's the strange part. Her voice is perfectly calm, and very gentle, the voice she'd use to tell a client their budget doesn't add up." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Is it the box?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

For the first time since this started, she's ahead of me. She sat at her desk for three nights and did the work, quietly, the way she does everything, and walked into my office with the proof in her hand. She's waiting to see what I'll do with it, and for a moment I honestly don't know.

<<linkreplace "Decide">>
<div id="cal-choice" class="choices">
<div><<link "Tell her part of the truth">><<replace "#cal-choice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Yes. It's the box, though not the white one in the meeting room, there's a stronger one. It makes people feel what they're already close to feeling, just a little more easily." },
{ text: "I tell her about the evenings, the sessions, the unit in the office. I don't tell her about her old job, or the sabotage, or why she was fired. She doesn't need that part. Nobody does." },
{ who: $mom, text: "And the nights I came up to your room?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Some of them." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Which ones?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Honestly, I don't know anymore. I stopped keeping track at some point." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She takes the printout back and looks at it for a long time. Then she folds it in half, and in half again, and holds it in both hands.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "I need to think about this, honey. I'm going to go sit in the meeting room for a while, and I'd like it if you didn't come in." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She's in there for two hours. Through the glass I can see her sitting at the end of the table, very straight, with the folded paper in front of her. She doesn't cry, and she doesn't call anyone. At one point she gets up and waters Gerald through the doorway, and sits down again.

At lunch she comes back to my desk and sits down in the same chair.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "I can't tell how much of this is me and how much is the box." },
{ text: "She turns the folded paper over in her fingers." },
{ who: $mom, text: "And I think... I think I've decided I don't care." },
{ who: $player, text: "You don't care?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "I sat in there and tried to be angry, honey. I really tried. And all I could think was that I've never been this happy. Not even close. If a box did that, then thank God for the box." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She drops the folded calendar in my wastebasket on her way back to her desk, without looking at it.

<<set $mom.flags.calendarChoice to "truth">>
<<UpdateStat "-" "MomResistance" 10>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 3>>
<<Feel $mom "player" 2 "lasting">>
<<AdvanceCorruptionStage $mom "She worked out the pattern on her own and asked me if it was the box. I told her part of the truth. She thought about it for two hours and decided she doesn't care.">>
<<ProfileLog $mom "The Calendar" "She found the pattern in the company calendar on her own: her bad days line up with the sessions and the days the office feels warm. She asked me if it was the box, and I told her part of the truth, not about her old job. She thought about it for two hours. Then she said she can't tell how much of this is her and how much is the box, and that she's decided she doesn't care.">>
<div class="navigation-link"><<link "That night" "The Calendar 2">><<AdvanceTimeTo 5>><</link>></div>
<</replace>><</link>></div>
<div><<if _calAnchorOk>><<link "Use the Anchor">><<replace "#cal-choice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Come with me for a second." },
{ text: "I take her into the meeting room and close the blinds. She lets me, the way she always lets me, and sits down at the table with her hands folded. The Anchor is in my jacket pocket, warm from my body." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<run setup.useDevice("valenxAnchor", "mom", 10, "mom_calendar")>>
<<DevicePulse 10>>

I take it out and point it at her and press the button, and say the sentence I've been carrying around for two weeks, slowly, so every word goes in.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "This is your choice. And you love it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

The coil whines. Her pupils go wide, all at once, like someone turned out a light behind her eyes. For three seconds she doesn't blink.

Then a thin line of blood runs out of her left nostril and over her lip, and she lifts her hand and touches it and looks at the red on her fingertips, puzzled, as if it belongs to someone else.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, look at that, how silly of me. I haven't been drinking enough water again, I always get these when I forget." },
{ text: "I hand her a tissue. She dabs her lip and smiles at me over it, a soft, clear, untroubled smile. The printout is still lying on the table between us. She glances at it as if it's somebody else's grocery list." },
{ who: $mom, text: "What was it I wanted to show you? Oh, it doesn't matter, it's nothing that can't wait." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I love working here, you know that, honey? I chose all of this, and I'd choose it again tomorrow." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She folds the printout in half and puts it in the recycling on her way out, and hums.

<<DevicePulse "off" "2s">>

Back at my desk, my hands are still not completely steady. I take out my phone and text $ethan.name, who is sitting forty feet away with his headphones on.

<i>Ever wonder what the dial really does at the top?</i>

The answer takes four minutes.

<i>Nope, and I'd like to keep it that way. More pressing issue: the coffee machine is making the dying-whale noise again, boss.</i>

He sends a whale emoji. I look across the office. He's looking at his screen. His screen is the device log, and I can see the shape of a single tall spike on it, reflected in the window behind him, before he clicks it away.

<<set $mom.flags.calendarChoice to "anchor">>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 5>>
<<Feel $mom "player" 2 "lasting">>
<<AdvanceCorruptionStage $mom "She worked out the pattern on her own and asked me if it was the box. I took her into the meeting room and used the Anchor. Now she believes it's her choice, and that she loves it.">>
<<ProfileLog $mom "The Calendar" "She found the pattern in the company calendar on her own and asked me if it was the box. I took her into the meeting room and used the Anchor: this is your choice, and you love it. Her nose bled. She said she hadn't been drinking enough water, threw the printout away and told me she'd choose this again.">>
<div class="navigation-link"><<link "That night" "The Calendar 2">><<AdvanceTimeTo 5>><</link>></div>
<</replace>><</link>><<else>><span class="offer-card locked" style="display:inline-flex"><span class="offer-label">Use the Anchor</span><span class="offer-lock"><<if !_calAnchor.owned>>I don't have it yet<<elseif setup.deviceUsesLeft(_calAnchor) <= 0>>It has no uses left<<else>>It needs a full charge<</if>></span></span><</if>></div>
</div>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>


:: The Calendar 2 [event mom_quest] {"position":"4900,1075","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Calendar" (mom_calendar), part 2: that night, the hallway. The device stays in my drawer, and I test what she
   promised. "Whatever you need." I make her leave my door open, with $sister.callName awake down the hall, and let her
   decide what I need; she leads for the first time. EXPLICIT blocks are left for the author.
   Advances her line; its set unlocks Whenever ($mom.flags.freeUse). */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[0].img>><</silent>>
I leave the devices in my desk drawer, all of them, and go out into the hallway at eleven in my socks.

She's coming out of the bathroom in her robe with her hair wrapped in a towel. She stops when she sees me. The hallway is dark except for the night light by the stairs, the one she put in when we were small and never took out.

She doesn't ask what I want. She looks at my face, and then she unties the towel and lets her hair down, and takes a step toward me.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Whatever you need, honey." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

There's no box switched on, no dial turned, and she hasn't made a single rule about it.

<<linkreplace "Take her to my room">>
I take her hand and lead her back to my room, and she comes without a sound, past $sister.callName's door, with her free hand holding the robe closed. There's light under that door, and the tinny sound of a video playing on a laptop.

I go in ahead of her and sit down on the edge of my bed. She comes in after me and reaches back for the door handle, out of habit.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Leave it open." },
{ text: "Her hand stops on the handle. She looks down the hallway, at the strip of light and the little voices from the laptop, and back at me." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Honey, she's right there, she's still up, if she so much as goes to brush her teeth she'll..." },
{ text: "She hears herself and stops. Then she lets go of the handle, and the door swings back against the wall on its own, the way it always has, because nobody ever fixed that either." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Open, then." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<if $mom.flags.calendarChoice === "anchor">>
She says it lightly, almost cheerfully, and comes over to me with that clear, untroubled look she's had all day, as if an open door were a thing she'd decided on herself, a long time ago, and was glad about.
<<else>>
She says it slowly, like a decision she's writing down so she can't lose it. Her eyes are perfectly clear. Whatever she worked out in the meeting room at lunch, she's still holding on to it.
<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Let her decide">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "You said whatever I need. So show me. What do you think I need?" },
{ text: "She thinks about it seriously, the way she'd think about what to make for dinner when somebody's had a bad day." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I think you need somebody who doesn't make you ask, sweetheart. You've had to ask for every little thing your whole life, from everyone, and I was one of them, wasn't I? I made you ask me for things I should have just given you." },
{ who: $player, text: "Sometimes." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Well. Not anymore." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She unties the robe and lets it drop on my floor, next to my shoes, and doesn't pick it up.

/* EXPLICIT 1, she leads. The first time she takes the initiative without being told what to do: she undresses him,
   then goes down on him without being asked (her mouth, which she learned at The Crawl, but this time unordered), and
   after a while climbs onto him and has sex with him on his bed, her on top. He lets her set the pace; he barely
   moves at first. The open door: she glances at it a few times in the beginning, then stops. Her mood: no nerves, no
   apology, a kind of relief at not having to decide whether she's allowed. */
<<Media "images/characters/mom/events/the_calendar/night_0.mp4" 600>>
/* His room, the door open to the dark hallway, the night light by the stairs, Mom kneeling in front of him on the bed's edge */

<<linkreplace "Listen to the house">>
Down the hall the laptop goes quiet. $sister.callName's bed creaks, and then her light goes out, and the strip under her door goes dark.

Not that long ago, in her own bed, $mom.callName froze at a creak in the floorboards and stayed rigid until the pipes knocked. Tonight she hears the bed and the light switch, and she looks at the open door, and then she looks back down at me and doesn't stop at all.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "She's asleep. Or she isn't, and either way, I don't..." },
{ text: "She doesn't finish the sentence. I don't think she was ever going to." },
{ who: $player, text: "You don't what?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "I don't mind, honey. That's the funny part. I keep waiting to mind, and I don't." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

/* EXPLICIT 2, the middle. She keeps going, on top of him, and talks to him the whole time in the low voice, not about
   herself anymore but about him: how good he's been, how hard he works, that he never has to ask. She asks him what he
   wants once, he tells her, she does it at once (one change of position, his choice). Neither of them is quiet about it
   the way they were in her bed. */
<<Media "images/characters/mom/events/the_calendar/night_1.mp4" 600>>
/* On his bed, her on top, the hallway dark behind the open door */

<<linkreplace "Let her finish it">>
/* EXPLICIT 3, the finish. Him first this time, and she makes sure of it, because that's what she decided he needs.
   Whether she comes too is up to you; if she does, it's after, and almost an afterthought to her, which says
   something. The text below picks up after. */

Afterwards she doesn't ask me to stay with her, and she doesn't ask if it was all right. She lies next to me for a minute with her hand flat on my chest, getting her breath back, and then she sits up and starts looking for her robe.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "What time do you want your coffee tomorrow? You've got that call at nine, so I was thinking half past seven, unless you'd rather sleep in a little and then I'll just bring it up at eight and we'll see." },
{ who: $player, text: "Seven-thirty is fine." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Seven-thirty, then." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She ties the robe, once, not twice, and goes. In the doorway she stops and looks back at the door, swung all the way open against the wall.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Open or closed, honey?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Leave it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She leaves it. I listen to her walk down the hall, past $sister.callName's dark door, and she doesn't hurry and she doesn't tiptoe. The night light by the stairs is still on.

<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 2>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "MomLust" 20>>
<<NextQuest $mom>>
<<ReturnFromEvent "Continue" "Bedroom">>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
